      "problem": "Given that $‖2u+v‖=14$ and $‖u‖=3$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v‖ & \\le 2‖u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v‖ & \\le 2‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le 2\\cdot 3+‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le 6+‖v‖ \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $8.$",
